# Auto Voice Channels: example configuration.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the three required values. Never commit a real `.env`.
# Everything else is optional and has a working default.
# Full guide: https://auto-voice.io/docs/self-hosting

# --- Required ---

# Developer Portal > Bot > Reset Token. Keep it secret.
DISCORD_TOKEN=
# Developer Portal > General Information > Application ID.
CLIENT_ID=
# `docker compose up` sets this for you and ignores what is here. Only needed if
# you run the bot some other way.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/avc

# --- Worth setting ---

# A text channel id. The bot posts errors it could not handle there. Without it
# they only reach the container logs, where nobody sees them.
# ADMIN_CHANNEL_ID=

# The only way to find out your bot has died. The bot POSTs this URL every minute
# while it is healthy, and whatever is on the other end tells you when the POSTs
# stop. Any free heartbeat monitor works (healthchecks.io, UptimeRobot, Better
# Stack): create a heartbeat check, paste its URL here, and give it a grace window
# of at least 5 minutes. It also stops pinging when the bot is running but not
# working, so a missed beat means "look at this", not just "the process exited".
# WATCHDOG_PING_URL=

# --- AI-assisted templates (optional) ---

# `/templateassistant` lets admins describe the channel names they want in plain
# language and writes the template for them. Setting a key is the whole switch.
# The command is not even registered without one.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions endpoint works:
#   OpenAI       https://api.openai.com/v1        (the default)
#   OpenRouter   https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   Ollama       http://localhost:11434/v1        (any key value, it ignores it)
# AVC_AI_API_KEY=
# AVC_AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# AVC_AI_MODEL=gpt-5.4-mini

# --- Backups (optional) ---

# Scheduled pg_dump to any S3-compatible bucket (Backblaze B2, Cloudflare R2, AWS
# S3, MinIO), taken by the bot itself, so there is nothing extra to run. Set all
# five or none: a half-set group is a startup error rather than a silent disable,
# because a typo that quietly turned backups off would only surface at restore time.
# BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.us-west-002.backblazeb2.com
# BACKUP_S3_REGION=us-west-002
# BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=
# BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Client-side AES-256-GCM, so the storage provider cannot read your data.
# 32 bytes: `openssl rand -base64 32`. Strongly recommended, and LOSING IT LOSES
# THE BACKUPS, with no way to find out until you try to restore. Keep a copy
# somewhere other than the machine it protects.
# BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Defaults: daily at 03:00 UTC, keeping 7 daily / 4 weekly / 6 monthly, with a
# weekly restore drill. See the docs to change any of it.

# --- Rarely needed ---

# A test server id. Slash commands register to just that server and appear
# instantly, instead of taking up to an hour to go global. Leave blank normally.
# DEV_GUILD_ID=
# Guards GET /diagnostics, which exposes shard topology and every runtime flag.
# Unset leaves it open, which is usually fine on a box only you can reach. Set it
# and callers must send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Minimum 16 characters.
# DIAGNOSTICS_TOKEN=
# Discord requires sharding above 2500 servers. One instance claims every shard,
# so this is the only value to change if you ever get there.
# TOTAL_SHARDS=1
# trace | debug | info | warn | error | fatal | silent
# LOG_LEVEL=info
